course: dictionary
lesson: 4721
title: Hope and its many shades
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Hope can be a verb, a noun or an adjective, so look at the words around it. «I hope you feel better» uses hope as a verb: you want something good to happen. «She has high hopes for the test» uses hopes as a noun: something you wish for.
explain: Context tells you whether hope is good news or bad. «Some Christians hope God will make all creation new» shows hope as a wish about the future. Hopeful means full of hope, and hopeless means having no hope at all.
explain: Hope is not the same as knowing. Scientists do not just hope their results are right; they check them. Hope is about wanting something good to happen, which is a different job from proving it.
fact: To hope means to want something to happen and to think it could happen.
fact: Hope is the feeling that something good may happen.
fact: «I hope so» means I want it to be true; «I hope not» means I don't want it to be true.
fact: Useful phrases: hope for, high hopes, give up hope, lose hope, hope for the best.
fact: «Prophets ... gave hope in hard times»: prophets were messengers who spoke God's word, and they comforted people when life was hard.
exercise: «I hope you feel better soon,» says Mum. What does hope mean here? | *You want something good to happen | You are certain it will happen | You are angry with someone | You want to forget something
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Disappointment is the feeling when things turn out worse than you hoped.» | feeling | normal | *hoped | disappointment
exercise: Lee says he has no hope of winning. Which word means having no hope at all? | hopeful | hopes | *hopeless | hoping
test: «I hope not,» said Sam. What does Sam mean? | He wants it to be true | He is very hungry | *He does not want it to be true | He is certain it will happen
test: Which phrase means you have stopped believing things will get better? | hope so | hope for the best | *give up hope | high hopes
exam: Why do scientists check their results instead of just hoping they are right? | *Hope is not proof, so they must check | They never check their results | They enjoy waiting for answers | Hope is always right in science
